# Static assets served by Workers static assets (no Worker code runs): same base security headers as the Worker
# (workers/security.ts) and the Vercel deployment. HTML is server-rendered by the Worker, which adds the nonce CSP.
# No CSP here: a service worker inherits the CSP of its own script response, and a restrictive one blocks its fetches.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), geolocation=(self)

# Build output under /assets/ is content-hashed (every file name carries a hash), so it never changes in place:
# cache it for a year. HTML (server-rendered), sw.js, the web manifest and everything else keep the default
# revalidating cache, so a deploy is picked up on the next load.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
